QMacStyle: Fix invisible check boxes in item views

Backport of qtbase 774ebf546bec0c184d2760df84714fd8742e75b5 (dev, picked
to 6.12 as 39c36a08509f711cd9d321ddd7fc0afdec495894, QTBUG-150017), which
is not in 6.8.5.

drawNSViewInRect() hands its draw block a rect in the coordinates of the
view's superview, and the check box indicator drew its cell into that
rect as is. For check boxes in item views off the first row or column
the cell then ended up outside its view, and with Liquid Glass it was not
visible. The context is now translated to the origin of the rect, and
the cell is drawn into the bounds of the view.

Unlike the other QMacStyle patches here, this one is not limited to
Liquid Glass, but the old look renders byte for byte as with 6.8.5.

--- a/qtbase/src/plugins/styles/mac/qmacstyle_mac.mm
+++ b/qtbase/src/plugins/styles/mac/qmacstyle_mac.mm
@@ -3434,8 +3434,8 @@
             return cs == QStyleHelper::SizeSmall ? 0.5 : 0.0;
         } ();
         d->drawNSViewInRect(tb, opt->rect, p, ^(CGContextRef ctx, const CGRect &rect) {
-            CGContextTranslateCTM(ctx, 0, vOffset);
-            [tb.cell drawInteriorWithFrame:rect inView:tb];
+            CGContextTranslateCTM(ctx, rect.origin.x, rect.origin.y + vOffset);
+            [tb.cell drawInteriorWithFrame:tb.bounds inView:tb];
         });
         break; }
     case PE_FrameFocusRect:
